    {
      "id": "claim_1dcdba50374f422b89ea72996593f294",
      "statement": "The GasBee nRF's ~100mA (0.1C) charge current is a calculated target set by holding HICHG (P0.13) low via a gpio-hog so two 2.7kOhm resistors parallel the BQ25101 ISET pin; the actual delivered charge current has not yet been measured on hardware, and firmware must never drive HICHG high.",
      "evidence": [
